\begin{align*}
(a+b)^n=\sum_{r=0}^n\binom{n}{r}a^{n-r}b^r
\end{align*}
in which $(a+b)^n=(x-1)^9$, $n=9$, $a=x$, and $b=-1$.  We plug it in, and find
\begin{align*}
&= \binom{9}{0} x^9(-1)^0+\binom{9}{1}x^8(-1)+\binom{9}{2}x^7(-1)^2+\cdots +\binom{9}{8}x^1(-1)^8\\
